    <div class="stat">2.3M+</div>
    <div class="stat-label">international patients (2024)</div>
    <p style="margin-top:10px;color:#4a5568;line-height:1.6;font-size:.92rem;">The established brand. Standardized processes, strong hospitality integration, multilingual service. Best for: cosmetic surgery, dental, IVF. Cardiac/ortho quality is mid-tier.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="market-card">
    <div class="flag">🇲🇾</div>
    <h3>Malaysia</h3>
    <div class="stat">1.6M</div>
    <div class="stat-label">international patients (2024)</div>
    <p style="margin-top:10px;color:#4a5568;line-height:1.6;font-size:.92rem;">The value choice for Indonesians. Good cardiac and orthopedic programs. Prices ~⅓ of Western rates. Weakness: limited oncology depth, fewer clinical trials.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="market-card">
    <div class="flag">🇸🇬</div>
    <h3>Singapore</h3>
    <div class="stat">646K</div>
    <div class="stat-label">international patients (2024)</div>
    <p style="margin-top:10px;color:#4a5568;line-height:1.6;font-size:.92rem;">The premium option. Highest JCI density in Asia. Best for: complex cancer, pediatric oncology, bone marrow transplant. Pricing close to Western private care.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="market-card">
    <div class="flag">🇨🇳</div>
    <h3>China</h3>
    <div class="stat">1.28M</div>
    <div class="stat-label">international patients (2025 est.)</div>
    <p style="margin-top:10px;color:#4a5568;line-height:1.6;font-size:.92rem;">The rising contender. World-leading in cardiac surgery volume, CAR-T cancer therapy, orthopedics. Price advantage is significant. Weakness: less tourism infrastructure, language barrier (mitigated by international departments).</p>
  </div>
</div>

